{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/shaft-verifier-spec.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# Leaf spec: Input Shaft runtime verifier (producer)\n\nObjective: an independent real-browser verifier for the integrated Input Shaft inspection that proves or disproves gates G4 (shaping, slowdown, stock removal, completion, exact cards) and G5 (hobbing, support comparison, assembled finale, exact restoration) with same-session telemetry plus rendered frames. Never weaken a check to pass; report real app defects with file:line.\n\nFiles you own (create only): scripts/verify-shaft-inspection.mjs, project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/runtime/shaft/ (outputs + README.md), project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/gates/shaft-runtime-browser.md (create; S1..S8 below; check only with evidence). Do not modify src/, other scripts, public/ or other evidence. Others' work is in progress: never revert or stage; no git; do not read TODO.md or queue docs.\n\nRead: docs/jgun-manufacturing-inspection-plan.md sections 2, 4, 8 (the validation packet), project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/lifecycle-contract.md section 9 (telemetry), src/scene/inspection/shaft/{story,script,schedule,kinematics,shaftRuntime}.ts (beats, card schedule, telemetry fields under window.__inspection.shaft), src/components/RingInspection.tsx and ShaftStoryLayer.tsx (DOM: trigger \"Inspect the input shaft\", dialog, seek slider #inspection-seek, chapter buttons \"Why the groove was needed\" / \"Material attempts\" / \"Changing the process\" / \"Moving the supports\", Play sequence / Pause / Replay / \"Return to narrative\", card DOM [data-shaft-card], [data-shaft-attribution], [data-shaft-recap], [data-shaft-stress], polite status [data-shaft-status]), scripts/verify-manufacturing-inspection.mjs (established Playwright setup, restore comparison, census, pixel statistics; reuse its patterns), project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/runtime/shaft-smoke/smoke.mjs (a parent smoke probe that already enters and seeks successfully).\n\nCases (desktop 1440x900 and narrow 390x844; chromium channel chrome with the same flags as the existing verifiers; ?chapter=1&inspectionProof=1):\nS1 Entry/readiness: loading -> compiling -> ready from both blueprint and exploded narrative modes (buttons /BLUEPRINT WIREFRAME/ and /EXPLODED ASSEMBLY/); Play disabled before ready; the core bundle requested once per session (full tier: manufacturing-core-full.glb); zero console/page errors (record warnings separately; THREE.Clock deprecation and D3D shader precision X4122 warnings are known).\nS2 Shaping (G4): forward sweep 0..15 s at <=0.05 s via the seek slider: shaft.teethFormed non-decreasing and reaching 10 by 15.0 s; teethPartial equals the count of retained spaces with 0 < depth < 1, including return strokes; no new depth is added during return, active engagement is absent during return, and the current engaged space retains its previous-pass depth ahead of the cutter leading face; cutter visible within 2..15 and absent outside its fade; chip visible only while the cutter is cutting; at the slow-exit window (read 7.2..9.6 from kinematics constants or telemetry) the cutter leading face passes beyond the last tooth material into the groove (telemetry edge/stroke values vs 9.875 mm) and the camera is stable (camera matrix constant across 3 frames while paused at those times).\n\nOctober 6 S2 semantic correction: the original phrase \"teethPartial only while cutting\" conflated persistent partly machined stock with active removal. Preview run 1 records the original failures. The accepted four-pass progression retains previous-pass depths; zeroing them on return would misrepresent the model. Fresh Z.ai GLM review of the actual runtime/kinematics/shader snippets returns FIX-CONTRACT, request `chatcmpl-19239f8e910f4a52a456ddee`, HTTP 200, observed response model `zai/glm-5.3`. The replacement adds causal no-removal/engagement/shader-mask checks rather than exempting return from verification. Read `shaft-partial-depth-contract-review-2026-10-06.md`; do not rewrite the original failed run.\nS3 Cards (G4): at times inside each material beat assert the exact DOM strings character for character (\"AISI 4140 (40-45 HRC)\", \"AISI 4340 (48-50 HRC)\", \"C300 (56-58 HRC)\", then \"AISI 4340 (H.T. 48-50 HRC)\" with no FAILED), FAILED stamp present only after the readable interval, attribution present 15..22.6, \"Illustrative stress concentration\" present with warm stress 15..25 and cool stress from 32.8, recap caption 11..15; telemetry shaft.card.id/stamp and shaft.stress.kind agree with the DOM; no FEA numbers anywhere in the dialog text.\nS4 Hobbing (G5): hob visible 25..32 and not visible at >= 32.0; approved shaft teeth complete by 32; between 32 and 32.8 no tool and no stress overlay.\nS5 Supports and finale (G5): shaft.supports.deltaYmm within 2.75 +-0.005, endpointHeld during the hold; finale.assembled true and shaftCount 1 at >= 40; narrative alpha 0 and narrative meshes hidden throughout after the entry fade.\nS6 Seek/replay determinism: each chapter button lands on its chapter start with matching telemetry; direct seek vs continuous play (play ~1 s from a chapter start, pause, then seek the same time) give equal telemetry digests for the deterministic fields; Replay resets to 0.\nS7 Restore and census: Return and Escape from blueprint and exploded entries restore camera matrix (delta <= 1e-6), projection, material mode/stage/scroll/focus exactly as the lifecycle verifier does; three warmed shaft enter/play/Return cycles show no growth in renderer.info.memory geometries/textures/programs (window.__threeRenderer) after return.\nS8 Rendered evidence: screenshots at one time per beat (isolate, shaping, slow exit, recap, materials, revised blank, hobbing, runout, supports, finale) per viewport, with canvas-region statistics (luma stddev, non-modal fraction) proving nonblank renders, from the same settled playhead/session as the telemetry; plus reduced-motion and poster shaft entry: static shaft view (.shaft-static) with transcript, zero manufacturing-core requests.\nAlso record (report only, no gate) rAF frame-interval percentiles while playing 2..15 and 25..32 on desktop.\n\nRun against the Vite dev server http://localhost:5199 while developing (do not restart it); the parent will run the final pass against a rebuilt production preview on :4173. Command: node scripts/verify-shaft-inspection.mjs --url=http://localhost:5199 --out=project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/runtime/shaft. Run it to completion twice; results must agree. Final message: changed paths, command, per-case results with deciding numbers, app defects (file:line) separated from harness limitations.\nREASONING: high\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
